  "verdict": "MECHANISM-FLOOR",
  "verdict_reason": "No bucket matched exactly. R-QP3 (D_med*=0.0947) and R-QPGEN (D_med*=0.0728) plateau within MECHANISM-FLOOR's [0.06,0.12] band; R-CATGEN (D_med*=0.1451) falls just outside it, driven by frame93/201 argmin sitting at the grid's lowest tested g=0.20 - the true CATGEN kernel optimum may lie below the grid floor, unexplored. Reported as the closest bucket. Important caveat (see lab-report-94.md 'anti-correlation finding'): for all 3 R-CATGEN frames, markov_score is still monotonically decreasing at the grid's top edge (g=1.15, markov down to 0.060-0.115, better than any other variant's minimum) while D_born is best at low g - the two optima sit at opposite ends of the tested grid, so the frozen D_born-argmin decision rule understates R-CATGEN's markov-axis performance. H-mechanism is well-supported for the kernel residual; H-reservoir is not ruled out for the markov residual.",
